$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl (2Z)-(8-nitro-2H-1,5-benzoxathiepin-3(4H)- ylidene)ethanoate (17)
To a stirred solution of 0.3 g t-BuOK (2.6 mmol) in 15 cm3 THF at 0 °C
was added 0.44 cm3 triethylphosphonoacetate (2.2 mmol). After stirring
for 15 min, a solution of 0.45 g ketone 5 (2 mmol) in 10 cm3 THF was
added dropwise. The reaction mixture was stirred at 30 °C for 1 h,
quenched with saturated aqueous solution of sodium bicarbonate and
extracted with EtOAc. The extract was washed with brine, dried over
MgSO4, filtered, and evaporated. The residue was crystalized from EtOH,
filtered, and dried. Yellow solid; yield 76 %; m.p.: 105- 106 °C (EtOH);
1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 400 MHz): δ = 7.85 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H, H-7), 7.77 (s,
1H, H-9), 7.45 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H, H-6), 6.06 (s, 1H, CH), 5.37 (s, 2H,
2-CH2), 4.18 (s, 2H, 4-CH2), 4.10 (q, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H, CH2CH3), 1.20 (t, J
= 6.8 Hz, 3H, CH2CH3) ppm; 13C NMR (DMSO-d6, 100 MHz): δ = 165.7, 157.1,
156.8, 146.0, 137.9, 129.5, 119.7, 118.2, 116.8, 74.0, 60.8, 34.7, 14.7
ppm; IR (KBr): ν = 1697 (CO), 1521 (NO2), 1341 (NO2) cm-1. C13H13NO5S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Horner-Wadsworth-Emmons olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel synthesis of 2H-1,5-benzoxathiepin-3(4H)-one and
5H-4,1-benzoxathiepin-3(2H)-one derivatives and chemical properties
evaluation
